er|butter]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:egg|egg]]s, well beaten\n* ⅓ cup [[Cookbook:milk|milk]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:vanilla|vanilla]]\n\n=== Topping ===\n* ¾ cup butter, melted\n* 1 cup light [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:flour|flour]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:pecan|pecan]]s, [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# Blend all the base ingredients together until creamy and smooth.\n# Mix all the topping ingredients together in a bowl.\n# Transfer the sweet potato mixture to a large [[Cookbook:Baking Dish|casserole dish]].\n# Sprinkle on topping, and [[Cookbook:Baking|bake]] at 350°F until top crisps and hardens.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n* Other nuts can be used in the topping—[[Cookbook:almond |almonds]] or [[Cookbook:peanut |peanuts]] serve admirably.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sweet potato]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using light brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cow milk]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Sweet Potato Crisp","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"7 cups cooked, mashed sweet potatoes","sourceText":"7 cups cooked, mashed sweet potatoes","amountText":"7 cups cooked, mashed sweet potatoes","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 cup white granulated sugar","sourceText":"1 cup white granulated sugar","amountText":"1 cup white granulated sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"¾ cup butter","sourceText":"¾ cup butter","amountText":"¾ cup butter","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 eggs, well beaten","sourceText":"2 eggs, well beaten","amountText":"2 eggs, well beaten","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBind